Day 41–50: Server-side with Python Flask & REST APIs  

Topic:  
Python Flask is a lightweight web framework used to build web applications and APIs. REST APIs enable communication between client and server using HTTP methods, facilitating data exchange in web and mobile applications.  

Learning Objectives:  
• Understand Flask framework basics.  
• Design and develop RESTful APIs.  
• Integrate APIs with databases for data handling.  

Activities / Deliverables:  
• Set up a Flask environment.  
• Create RESTful endpoints for CRUD operations.  
• Integrate APIs with MongoDB.  

Important Concepts:  
• REST architecture and HTTP methods.  
• Flask routing and request handling.  
• JSON data interchange format.  

SQL Syntax / Commands:  
• `@app.route()` for defining endpoints.  
• `request.get_json()` for handling JSON data.  
• `jsonify()` for returning JSON responses.  

Real-world Use Cases:  
• Building backend services for mobile apps.  
• Creating APIs for IoT devices.  
• Developing microservices for scalable applications.  

Tools / Technologies:  
• Python Flask.  
• Postman (API testing tool).  
• MongoDB (for database integration).  

Summary:  
This module covered Flask framework and REST API development. Participants learned to design APIs, integrate them with databases, and handle HTTP requests, enhancing their backend development skills.  

