Day 51–60: Capstone Project — Volyo Student Portal  

Topic:  
The capstone project involves developing a student portal using MongoDB for the database and Flask for the backend. The portal will manage student data, course enrollment, and academic records.  

Learning Objectives:  
• Apply MongoDB and Flask skills in a real-world project.  
• Design and implement a functional student portal.  
• Ensure data security and efficient database management.  

Activities / Deliverables:  
• Design the portal’s database schema.  
• Develop REST APIs for student and course management.  
• Test and deploy the completed portal.  

Important Concepts:  
• Database schema design for scalability.  
• Secure API authentication mechanisms.  
• Deployment strategies for web applications.  

SQL Syntax / Commands:  
• `db.createCollection()` for schema creation.  
• `db.collection.insertMany()` for bulk data insertion.  
• `db.collection.deleteOne()` for removing records.  

Real-world Use Cases:  
• Educational institutions managing student data.  
• Online learning platforms with course enrollment features.  
• Administrative tools for academic record keeping.  

Tools / Technologies:  
• MongoDB (database).  
• Python Flask (backend).  
• Docker (containerization for deployment).  

Summary:  
The capstone project consolidated MongoDB and Flask skills, enabling participants to build a functional student portal. The project emphasized database design, API development, and deployment, preparing interns for professional challenges.  

